**1. Why did you use Git?**

Git is a version control tool. 
I used Git to store source code, track changes, and manage different versions of the code. 
It also helps team members work together.

---

**2. What is Jenkins?**

Jenkins is a CI/CD automation tool. 
I used Jenkins to automatically build, test, and deploy applications. 
It reduces manual work and makes deployment faster.

---

**3. What is Docker?**

Docker is a containerization tool.  
It packages an application with all required dependencies into a container.  
It helps run applications easily in different environments.

---

**4. Why did you use Kubernetes?**

Kubernetes is a container orchestration tool. 
I used Kubernetes to deploy, manage, and scale Docker containers.  
It also helps in maintaining application availability.

---

**5. What is Terraform?**

Terraform is an Infrastructure as Code tool. 
I used Terraform to create and manage AWS resources automatically using configuration files.

---

**6. Why did you use AWS EC2?**

EC2 provides virtual servers in the cloud. 
I used EC2 to host and run my application.

---

**7. What is AWS S3?**

S3 is a storage service in AWS. 
I used S3 to store files, application data, and backup data.

---

**8. What is Linux?**

Linux is an operating system widely used for servers. 
I used Linux for managing users, permissions, installing packages, and configuring services like Apache and Tomcat.

---

**9. What is CI/CD?**

CI/CD means Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment. 
It helps automate the process of code building, testing, and releasing applications quickly.

---

**10. What was your role in the project?**

My role was to manage the DevOps process. 
I worked on Git, Jenkins, Docker, Kubernetes, Terraform, AWS, and Linux configuration. 
I created infrastructure, deployed the application, and managed the deployment process.
